+# Annual Training requirements
+
+The Training matrix and completed-session list remain separate. A matrix status
+never creates a completed session, date, participant list, or hours.
+
+## Operator behavior
+
+An annual matrix names its year in review and in Word/PDF output. Existing
+unscoped matrices remain labeled **year not recorded**; opening a report does not
+assign a year to their recorded statuses or rewrite shared records.
+
+When a retained matrix belongs to a different or unknown year, **Start YYYY
+requirements** explicitly switches to the report's selected year. For each
+selected site, it uses that year's saved matrix if one exists. Otherwise it
+copies the displayed roster and requirement names, resets every nonblank status
+to **Not recorded**, and preserves intentional blanks. Earlier annual and
+unscoped records remain unchanged. Excluded Training requires explicit inclusion
+before this action is available. Demonstration reports cannot publish a year
+transition into the shared registry.
+
+A fresh report without a pinned matrix reuses its exact year's selected-site
+records. Missing sites can copy an earlier annual roster, but not its completion
+statuses. Future-year records are not used to seed earlier years. This read-only
+preparation does not publish shared data; an explicit matrix edit saves it.
+When only legacy unscoped data exists, it stays unscoped until a year transition.
+
+Same-year rollover preserves the matrix and drops monthly session records as
+before. Cross-year rollover preserves a pinned matrix with its original year
+label until the explicit switch, rather than silently relabeling historical
+completion. Report notes, other tables and pictures are independent.
+
+## Persistence and conflict rules
+
+The existing versioned contract manifest keeps its `schema: 1` envelope and
+legacy `sites` map. An optional `years` map holds each explicit year's `sites`.
+Annual tables use `training:matrix:v2:YYYY`; legacy tables keep
+`training:matrix:v1`. No new ReportTable fields or bulk migration are required.
+
+Each save checks the existing contract revision and updates only selected sites
+inside the appropriate year. Historical JSON versions, other years, other sites
+and other contracts are preserved. The existing metadata budget applies before
+publication. A stale or interrupted year-switch action does not overwrite an
+intervening matrix edit; the operator must review it and activate again.
+
+## Verification boundaries
+
+Synthetic tests cover year identity, blank statuses, scoped reuse, bounded
+storage failure, CAS conflicts, native Streamlit AppTest controls, pending edits,
+snapshot restoration, rollover, derivative DOCX and real LibreOffice PDF output.
+The core arbitrary imported annual-table mapping and actual browser/assistive
+technology/genuine branded-report acceptance remain separate work under #459
+and #496. This change does not alter #524's current-month-first layout or
+#432's repeated session-add behavior.
